<Policy title="Affiliate disclosure and commercial policy" description="See how The MoneyGoal earns through paid links, how we disclose compensation and why payment does not establish product suitability or editorial ranking.">
<p>We may earn a commission when you use a clearly marked paid link and complete the provider’s qualifying action. The action can be an approved application, subscription or brokerage activity, depending on the agreement. A click alone is not income.</p>
<h2>Existing relationship</h2><p><a href="/partner">Our Alice Blue disclosure</a> explains the existing brokerage relationship and the conflict created by compensation tied to trading. We do not encourage frequent trading to increase commission.</p>
<h2>Other programs</h2><p>We research additional providers, but a public affiliate program does not mean we have been accepted. We activate links only after approval, country eligibility, allowed promotions and a verification deadline are recorded. Unapproved, paused and expired offers do not appear as paid recommendations.</p>
<h2>How comparisons work</h2><p>We identify fees, eligibility, exclusions and useful alternatives, including providers that do not pay us. We do not sell editorial ranking positions. Compensation is not evidence that a product suits a reader. Technical financial promotions requiring qualifications or creative approval stay on hold until those requirements are satisfied.</p>
<h2>Before applying</h2><p>Check current documents on the provider’s site. Costs, eligibility and availability change. Applications, identity checks, deposits and account support happen with the provider. Our tools and educational pages remain free whether or not you use a paid link.</p>
</Policy>
